Hi Konny, I checked the Bravo environment in Docker Swarm.

The admin service has Sentry environment variables configured (REACT_APP_SENTRY_DSN, REACT_APP_SENTRY_ENABLE, REACT_APP_SENTRY_ENV, REACT_APP_SENTRY_DEBUG, and REACT_APP_SENTRY_SAMPLE_RATE).

For portal-api, there are no Sentry-specific environment variables exposed directly. However, the service uses a Docker configuration file mounted at /app/config.json, which may contain its application-level Sentry settings.





docker service ls --format "{{.Name}}" | Select-String "bravo"



docker service ls --format "{{.Name}}" | Select-String "bravo.*(admin-api|portal-api)"



docker service inspect <service-name> --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Env}}'



docker service inspect wholeshestack_bravo_admin --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Env}}' | ConvertFrom-Json | Where-Object { $_ -match 'SENTRY' }



docker service inspect wholeshestack_bravo_portal-api --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Env}}' |
ConvertFrom-Json |
ForEach-Object { ($_ -split '=',2)[0] }







docker service inspect wholeshestack_bravo_portal-api --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Env}}' | ConvertFrom-Json | Where-Object { $_ -match 'SENTRY' }






docker service inspect wholeshestack_bravo_portal-api --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Configs}}'



docker service inspect wholeshestack_bravo_portal-api --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Secrets}}'








docker service inspect wholeshestack_bravo_portal-api --format '{{json .Spec.TaskTemplate.ContainerSpec.Configs}}' |
ConvertFrom-Json |
Select-Object ConfigName, @{Name='Target';Expression={$_.File.Name}}